+  # HarmonyOS uses musl libc.  We must NOT set define_xopen_source=no,
+  # because ncurses wide-character interfaces (cchar_t, setcchar, wadd_wch,
+  # etc.) require _XOPEN_SOURCE_EXTENDED or _XOPEN_SOURCE >= 500 to be
+  # visible in <ncurses.h> (NCURSES_WIDECHAR gating, see E033).
+  # Falling through to the default (define_xopen_source=yes) gives
+  # _XOPEN_SOURCE=700 on most systems, which is correct for musl.
+  # No special case needed — just let the default logic handle it.
 
